save(400,dict(paragraphs=["Heba Fatima writes poetry and literary criticism. Her published work identifies her as an English lecturer at Birupa College in Odisha, with interests in folklore, gender and popular culture. Her essay ‘The Reptile Within’ studies how contemporary Odia short stories revisit a Panchatantra fable; her criticism also includes a review of Steven Feld’s work on sound, song and mourning.","In Kabita Live, ‘Abandoned Homes’ makes domestic ruins and broken toys bear the weight of displacement and loss. ‘To My Velutha’ turns inward, addressing an absent beloved through images of water, memory and a grief that keeps growing. Both poems ask what remains of home when the people or future that gave it meaning are threatened."],sources=[source('Heba Fatima — Sound and Sentiment review, Northeast Popular Culture Association','https://www.northeastpca.org/post/book-review-sound-and-sentiment-birds-weeping-poetics-and-song-in-kaluli-expression-by-steven-f',['English lecturer at Birupa College; interests in folklore, gender and popular culture; published review']),source('The Reptile Within — journal article by Heba Fatima','https://ijhssm.org/issue_dcp/The%20Reptile%20Within%20%20A%20Study%20of%20Three%20Odia%20Short%20Stories%20in%20Light%20of%20The%20Story%20of%20the%20Monkey%20and%20the%20Crocodile%20from%20the%20Panchatantra.pdf',['2024 article authorship, lecturer affiliation, study of three Odia short stories and Panchatantra'])],identity_match='Captured Odisha English lecturer biography agrees with both article and NEPCA bylines; NEPCA explicitly links the Bhubaneswar/Birupa professional profile found in search.',poems_read=[dict(id=569,title='Abandoned Homes',basis='Full original read: house fragments, damaged toys, bones and homelands develop displacement and violence.'),dict(id=716,title='TO MY VELUTHA',basis='Full original read: addressed beloved, pregnant grief metaphor, river/shore imagery and uncertainty about tomorrow.')],limitations=['Employment described as published affiliation rather than independently confirmed current appointment.','No named conflict attributed to Abandoned Homes.','Velutha may be a literary allusion, but no unsupported specific character identification added.','Unrelated namesakes and their translation/education claims excluded; no books verified.'],next_action='Author/editor to confirm preferred biographical details and affiliation.'))
